Tell data-control clients when the selection is cleared

When the clipboard owner goes away (the app that copied exits) or a client
clears the selection, Hyprland told wl_data_device clients but not
wlr-data-control or ext-data-control ones. Clipboard managers and
`wl-paste --watch` never saw the clipboard empty, so they kept showing the
old contents and could not react, for example by keeping the last copy
alive after its app closed. Send the cleared selection to both data-control
protocols too, for the clipboard and the primary selection.

Backport of hyprwm/Hyprland#16117 (304bbec7df), merged after v0.56.2.

--- a/src/managers/SeatManager.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/SeatManager.cpp
@@ -643,8 +643,11 @@
     if (m_selection.currentSelection)
         m_selection.currentSelection->cancelled();
 
-    if (!source)
+    if (!source) {
         PROTO::data->setSelection(nullptr);
+        PROTO::dataWlr->setSelection(nullptr, false);
+        PROTO::extDataDevice->setSelection(nullptr, false);
+    }
 
     m_selection.currentSelection = source;
 
@@ -669,8 +672,11 @@
     if (m_selection.currentPrimarySelection)
         m_selection.currentPrimarySelection->cancelled();
 
-    if (!source)
+    if (!source) {
         PROTO::primarySelection->setSelection(nullptr);
+        PROTO::dataWlr->setSelection(nullptr, true);
+        PROTO::extDataDevice->setSelection(nullptr, true);
+    }
 
     m_selection.currentPrimarySelection = source;
 
